{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.FreeAlgebra","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.RingQuot","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.Coxeter.Basic"],"declarations":30,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.nontrivial_of_symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.nontrivial_of_symm","kind":"theorem","line":301,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.lean#L301-L310","doc":"**The Hecke algebra does not collapse.** Over a nontrivial base ring with a\nsymmetric Coxeter matrix, `0 ≠ 1` in `HeckeAlgebra R q M`.\n\nWithout this every theorem in this file would be vacuously true of the zero ring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.indexRep_ne_signRep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.indexRep_ne_signRep","kind":"theorem","line":288,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.lean#L288-L299","doc":"**The two extreme cell modules are distinct** whenever `q ≠ −1` and there is at\nleast one generator.\n\n`indexRep` and `signRep` are the `q`-analogues of the trivial and sign representations\nof `S_n`, i.e. the cell modules `S^{(n)}` and `S^{(1ⁿ)}`. At `q = −1` they coincide,\nwhich is the first place the semisimplicity of `H_n(q)` fails. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.signRep_T","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.signRep_T","kind":"theorem","line":284,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.lean#L284-L286","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.signRep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.signRep","kind":"def","line":274,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.lean#L274-L282","doc":"**The sign representation** `T_i ↦ −1`.\n\nThe other one-dimensional representation, and the second extreme cell module. Its\nquadratic check is even cheaper than `indexRep`'s: the *second* factor `(T_i + 1)`\nvanishes on the nose, so nothing about `q` is used. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.indexRep_T","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.indexRep_T","kind":"theorem","line":270,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.lean#L270-L272","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.indexRep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.indexRep","kind":"def","line":260,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.lean#L260-L268","doc":"**The index representation** `T_i ↦ q`.\n\nBoth relations are immediate: the quadratic factor `(q − q)` vanishes, and with every\ngenerator sent to the same scalar each side of a braid relation is a power of `q`, so\nsymmetry of `M` is exactly what makes the two exponents agree. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.exists_unique_lift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.exists_unique_lift","kind":"theorem","line":240,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.lean#L240-L247","doc":"**The universal property**, as a single `∃!`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.hom_ext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.hom_ext","kind":"theorem","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.lean#L222-L238","doc":"**Uniqueness.** Two `R`-algebra maps out of the Hecke algebra agreeing on every\ngenerator are equal.\n\n`RingQuot.mkAlgHom` is surjective, so it suffices that the composites agree; those are\nmaps out of a *free* algebra, so `FreeAlgebra.hom_ext` reduces that to the generators. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.lift_T","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.lift_T","kind":"theorem","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.lean#L214-L220","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.lift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.lift","kind":"def","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.lean#L198-L212","doc":"**Existence.** A family `f : B → A` satisfying both relations induces an\n`R`-algebra map out of the Hecke algebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.isUnit_T","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.isUnit_T","kind":"theorem","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.lean#L181-L192","doc":"**Each generator is a unit**, whenever the parameter is.\n\nSo the presentation really does factor through the braid group: every `T_i` has a\ntwo-sided inverse, and `σ_i⁻¹` in the skein dictionary denotes an actual element. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.sub_mul_T","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.sub_mul_T","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.lean#L168-L179","doc":"The same product in the other order. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.T_mul_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.T_mul_sub","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.lean#L149-L166","doc":"The quadratic relation, rearranged: `T_i (T_i − (q−1)) = q`.\n\nThis is the whole content of invertibility — over any ring in which `q` is a unit it\nexhibits `q⁻¹(T_i − (q−1))` as an inverse. The only step beyond expanding is that\n`algebraMap` is central. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.T_braid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.T_braid","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.lean#L134-L139","doc":"**The braid relation holds.** The alternating product of `M i j` factors starting\nwith `T_i` equals the alternating product of `M j i` factors starting with `T_j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.T_quadratic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.T_quadratic","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.lean#L128-L132","doc":"**The quadratic relation holds.** `(T_i − q)(T_i + 1) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.T","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.T","kind":"def","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.lean#L122-L124","doc":"The generator `T_i`, the image of the free generator `i` in the quotient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.instAlgebraHeckeAlgebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.instAlgebraHeckeAlgebra","kind":"instance","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.lean#L119-L120","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.instRingHeckeAlgebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.instRingHeckeAlgebra","kind":"instance","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.lean#L116-L117","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.HeckeAlgebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.HeckeAlgebra","kind":"def","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.lean#L112-L114","doc":"**The Iwahori–Hecke algebra** of the Coxeter matrix `M` over `R` at parameter `q`,\nin the Iwahori normalisation `(T_i − q)(T_i + 1) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.Rel.braid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.Rel.braid","kind":"ctor","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.lean#L106-L108","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.Rel.quadratic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.Rel.quadratic","kind":"ctor","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.lean#L104-L105","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.Rel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.Rel","kind":"inductive","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.lean#L97-L108","doc":"The two defining families of the Iwahori–Hecke algebra, as a relation on the free\nalgebra: the **quadratic** relation for each generator, and the **braid** relation for\neach ordered pair.\n\n`RingQuot` closes this up into a ring congruence, so listing the raw relations here is\nenough — there is no ideal to generate and no two-sided-span reasoning downstream. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.map_altProd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.map_altProd","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.lean#L80-L91","doc":"Any multiplicative map transports an alternating product.\n\nStated through `MonoidHomClass` rather than for a bare `A →* B`, so that it applies\ndirectly to the `AlgHom`s this file pushes relations along — `AlgHomClass` extends\n`RingHomClass` extends `MonoidHomClass`, so no manual `.toMonoidHom` is needed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.altProd_const","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.altProd_const","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.lean#L72-L78","doc":"An alternating product of a single element is just a power. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.altProd_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.altProd_three","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.lean#L69-L70","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.altProd_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.altProd_two","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.lean#L66-L67","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.altProd_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.altProd_one","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.lean#L63-L64","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.altProd_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.altProd_succ","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.lean#L60-L61","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.altProd_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.altProd_zero","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.lean#L58-L58","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.altProd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.altProd","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.lean#L49-L56","doc":"The alternating product `a · b · a · b ⋯` with `n` factors.\n\n`altProd a b 0 = 1`, `altProd a b 1 = a`, `altProd a b 2 = a * b`,\n`altProd a b 3 = a * b * a`, and so on. This is the shape both sides of a braid\nrelation take. ","signatureChunk":0}]}